  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 10,000 gp (lesser), 20,000 gp (normal), 40,000 gp (greater)<br>\n<strong>Weight</strong> 5 lbs.; <strong>Feat Cost</strong> 2 sp</p>\n<p>This effect only works on mind-affecting talents. A threnodic talents affects undead creatures (even mindless undead) as if they were not immune to mind-affecting effects, but has no effect on living creatures. This metamagic does not give you the effects of the Mind sphere’s Expanded Charm talent.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Apparatus, Threnodic Spell; <strong>Cost</strong> 5,000 gp (lesser), 10,000 gp (normal), 20,000 gp (greater)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic#toc56\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Selected profile: lesser tier; held slender rod. Apply as part of casting a qualifying sphere effect of caster level seven or lower. Hold this apparatus in at least one hand while applying it. Spend one of three daily uses; only one metamagic apparatus may apply per casting. Its feat's extra spell-point and casting-time costs are waived, but normal effect and other-metamagic costs still apply.</p><p>Only mind-affecting talents qualify. They affect undead, including mindless undead, as if not immune, and have no effect on living creatures. This does not grant Expanded Charm or ignore other targeting limits.</p><p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic\">Shared metamagic apparatus rules</a>. Feat Cost applies to taking the feat, not using the physical apparatus.</p>",
      "unidentified": ""
    },
